# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OPEN CONFIG
# Real values, safe to commit. Loaded via Bun's native process.env (this is
# a tooling script, not a SvelteKit app, so there's no $env module here).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The TaBiThA Cloudflare account id -- not sensitive on its own (an identifier, not a credential).
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=8582954a9e4c6f0259c6236be794d7d3

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRETS
# Left blank here; real values live only in .env.local (gitignored).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Create as an account token (Manage Account -> Account API tokens, not My Profile -> API Tokens),
# named "Notifications - tools/alerts apply", with two permissions on the TaBiThA account: Account >
# Notifications > Edit (the email policy) and Account > Workers Observability > Edit (the Issues
# automations that trigger it; labeled "Legacy" in the dashboard, still the one the API needs). Used
# by apply.ts to reconcile config.ts against the live account.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Normally left blank. Only read if apply.ts has to create a policy that doesn't exist -- e.g. after
# someone deletes it, or on a new Cloudflare account. Cloudflare won't create a policy without a
# recipient, and the dashboard can't create this policy type at all, so this is the recovery path.
# Comma-separated (e.g. "a@canil.ca,b@canil.ca"). Day-to-day, recipients are managed on the
# policy's dashboard page (see README). Kept out of the committed files because this repo is public.
ALERT_EMAILS=
